NXR-149|Three-worker PLAIN RISCue AXI UART simulation|Integration|The project shall provide a static three-worker UART demo executing actual firmware on the existing PLAIN RISCue AXI core with C# SharpTestBench serial verification.|Observe repeated work and preemption end to end instead of relying only on host kernel models.|Equal-priority workers retain independent arithmetic state; first records show all workers began during non-yielding work; decode physical UART bits and verify repeated per-thread sequence/results; detect fatal/unexpected traps; preserve exact source and binary identities; use no custom Python tooling.|Native C# runner, actual RV32 cross-build/allocation audit, Verilator execution and SharpTestBench UART arithmetic/preemption checks.|NXR-140,NXR-142|Optional RTOS_SIMULATION host tools; uart firmware preset with SYNC, LOGGING, METRICS, guards and round robin; PLAIN CPU and ordinary simulation RAM.|Three permanent 1536-byte worker stacks, 512-byte idle stack, fixed logger and 4096-byte boot reserve; measure the larger final demo separately from nano.|examples/axi_uart_threads.cpp,sim/rtl/riscue_demo.sv,sim/SharpDemo/Tests.cs,tools/NexRT.Sim/Program.cs,docs/uart-demo.rst|Source integrates existing external core and transmitter without editing them; RTL simulation is required and does not establish FPGA timing or physical board operation.|examples/axi_uart_threads.cpp,sim/rtl/riscue_demo.sv,sim/SharpDemo/Tests.cs,tools/NexRT.Sim/Program.cs|sim/SharpDemo/Tests.cs|PartialSourceUnverified
